 "notes": [
  "REDEEM A CODE, drawn on YOUR LORDSHIP's page (profile/page: the frame and header with everything inside cleared) -- the profile painting's own row has the page's envelope.",
  "The title is set where the painting's YOUR LORDSHIP stands, in its type at its size: Cinzel 700 at 56 is the painted title's width (458) and small capitals' height (35) to a unit.",
  "The code is typed into the painting's empty box (profile/box, nine-patched to the page's width); REDEEM and OPEN THE ROYAL MAIL are the kit's green plate, CLOSE the painting's own, in the middle of the foot.",
  "After a code is taken: the letter's title and what it carries (Art.reward_icon, as the mail rows draw it), five lines at most and a count of the rest, and the way to the mail.",
  "Stretch bands: plain panel between the blocks, most of the extra height above CLOSE.",
  "Every text rect is its line (or its sample's lines) centred on the plate or space it was set in: a label cannot be shorter than its lines, so a taller rect set the words' top where the rect's is and dropped them."
